    "['set protocols ospf area [area_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ospf 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ospf 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated configuration for Huawei device:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 1.1.1.1 0.0.0.0\\n  network 172.16.1.0 0.0.0.255\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Huawei, OSPF uses \"network\" commands to specify interfaces instead of directly listing interfaces like Juniper\\n2. The \"passive\" behavior is implicit for loopback interfaces in Huawei\\n3. The network statements use wildcard masks (inverse of subnet masks)', 'trans_template': 'ospf 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated configuration for Huawei device:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 1.1.1.1 0.0.0.0\\n  network 172.16.1.0 0.0.0.255\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Huawei, OSPF uses \"network\" commands to specify interfaces instead of directly listing interfaces like Juniper\\n2. The \"passive\" behavior is implicit for loopback interfaces in Huawei\\n3. The network statements use wildcard masks (inverse of subnet masks)', 'trans_template': 'area 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'network 1.1.1.1 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'network 1.1.1.1 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated configuration for Huawei device:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 1.1.1.1 0.0.0.0\\n  network 172.16.1.0 0.0.0.255\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Huawei, OSPF uses \"network\" commands to specify interfaces instead of directly listing interfaces like Juniper\\n2. The \"passive\" behavior is implicit for loopback interfaces in Huawei\\n3. The network statements use wildcard masks (inverse of subnet masks)', 'trans_template': 'network 1.1.1.1 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'network 172.16.1.0 0.0.0.255', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'network 172.16.1.0 0.0.